//! A port of the [Lark](https://github.com/lark-parser/lark) parsing toolkit to Rust.
//!
//! Grammars are written in Lark's grammar syntax, and are interpreted exactly as Lark 1.3.1 does: the trees, the
//! token types and positions, and the errors are the same. A shared conformance suite, generated by Python Lark,
//! checks this for this crate and its .NET and TypeScript siblings.

// Ported code keeps Lark's shapes (long parameter lists, nested collection types) to stay easy to compare.
#![allow(
    clippy::too_many_arguments,
    clippy::type_complexity,
    clippy::mutable_key_type,
    clippy::needless_range_loop
)]

